WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.550
Coding Exercise 5 asks you to make a temporary
change inside a

00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.738
transaction and then undo it The task is to change
MRN one

00:00:07.762 --> 00:00:11.350
zero zero five to age sixty use RETURNING to inspect
the temporary

00:00:11.375 --> 00:00:14.800
result roll the change back and then verify the
original age with

00:00:14.825 --> 00:00:19.638
the final SELECT The starter already includes BEGIN
and the final SELECT

00:00:20.525 --> 00:00:25.075
Add an UPDATE after BEGIN Set age to sixty target
the correct

00:00:25.088 --> 00:00:28.000
MRN in the WHERE clause and add RETURNING so you can
see

00:00:28.025 --> 00:00:33.112
the changed row Then add ROLLBACK before the final
SELECT When you

00:00:33.138 --> 00:00:37.925
run the exercise pay attention to the sequence of
results The UPDATE

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:42.200
should show age sixty The final SELECT should show
that the original

00:00:42.225 --> 00:00:47.088
age returned after the rollback If both results show
sixty check whether

00:00:47.112 --> 00:00:51.438
you used COMMIT by mistake or forgot ROLLBACK If the
update affects

00:00:51.462 --> 00:00:56.150
the wrong row recheck the MRN condition This
exercise is a good

00:00:56.162 --> 00:01:00.650
example of using transactions as a safety tool while
learning You can

00:01:00.675 --> 00:01:04.963
practice a realistic data change inspect it and then
intentionally undo it

00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:10.200
Remember the meaning BEGIN starts the unit RETURNING
lets you inspect ROLLBACK

00:01:10.225 --> 00:01:13.525
discards the change and the final SELECT verifies
the outcome
